<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Council of Troubles</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1567–1576</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Council of Blood</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Council of Troubles was a special tribunal set up in 1567 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fernando-alvarez-de-toledo-3rd-duke-of-alba">Duke of Alba</a>, governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> for Philip II, to punish those involved in the iconoclastic riots and resistance of 1566. Called the Council of Blood by its victims, it condemned more than a thousand people to death, among them the counts of Egmont and Horn, and confiscated the property of many more. Its terror helped drive the Netherlands into open revolt.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/council-of-troubles.jpg" alt="Council of Troubles" width="320" height="260" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Simon Frisius · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bor-Nederlantsche-oorloghen_MGG_1258.tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
